    <div class="pkg">
      <section class="pkg__block" id="what">
        <p class="pkg__kicker">the fine print, in green</p>
        <h2>what is this place?</h2>
        <p>
          In 1999 I drew <a href="/dancing-banana-gif-meme/">a little banana that never stopped dancing</a>.
          It has a park now &mdash; <strong>a free browser game</strong>, no account, and every banana
          walking around is a real visitor, live.
        </p>
        <p>
          The catch: <strong>the park can die.</strong> One shared health meter, always sinking. The night it
          opened I set it to 5% and sixty weeds &mdash; by morning, two regulars had it back at 100%.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="pkg__block" id="do">
        <p class="pkg__kicker">the loop</p>
        <h2>what do you actually do here?</h2>
        <div class="pkg__grid">
          <article class="pkg__card">
            <div class="pkg__thumb"><img src="/assets/park/g-sunflower.png" alt="a grown sunflower — park pixel sprite" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h3>plant</h3>
            <p>Seeds cost coins, grow on watered days, and wear your name on the stake.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pkg__card">
            <div class="pkg__thumb"><img src="/assets/park/g-soil-wet.png" alt="watered soil — park pixel sprite" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h3>water anybody&rsquo;s</h3>
            <p>The whole park runs on strangers watering each other&rsquo;s beds. +2 rep a pour.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pkg__card">
            <div class="pkg__thumb"><img src="/assets/park/c-strawberry-4.png" alt="a ripe strawberry bush — park pixel sprite" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h3>harvest</h3>
            <p>Ripe pays rep and pockets a seed for <a href="/homestead/">your homestead</a>. Some bushes fruit three times.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pkg__card">
            <div class="pkg__thumb"><img src="/assets/park/w-weed1.png" alt="a weed — park pixel sprite" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h3>tidy</h3>
            <p>Weeds, litter, pond scum &mdash; every piece cleared lifts the meter, every piece left holds it down.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pkg__card">
            <div class="pkg__thumb"><img src="/assets/park/e-egg.png" alt="a park egg — pixel sprite" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h3>find eggs</h3>
            <p>Healthy parks lay them; above 95% they can come out golden. First tap wins.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="pkg__card">
            <div class="pkg__thumb"><img src="/assets/park/ov-0.png" alt="Old Peel on his bench — park pixel sprite" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h3>meet the locals</h3>
            <p>Old Peel has opinions. Twelve bird species visit by health. Both shops are inside the world.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="pkg__block" id="health">
        <p class="pkg__kicker">the meter</p>
        <h2>how park health works</h2>
        <ul class="pkg__list">
          <li><strong>It sinks on its own.</strong> Watering, planting and tidying push it back.</li>
          <li><strong>Mess caps the ceiling.</strong> No 100% while there&rsquo;s litter on the grass or scum on the pond.</li>
          <li><strong>The park shows it.</strong> Below 60 the colour drains and the animals mope; above 80 the rare birds and the eggs come back.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="pkg__block" id="guide">
        <p class="pkg__kicker">the ladder</p>
        <h2>seeds, stars and the gardener</h2>
        <p>Every harvest climbs your gardener level; the level raises the seed shelf.</p>
        <table class="pkg__seeds">
          <thead><tr><th>seeds</th><th>stars</th><th>unlocked at</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>daisy</td><td>&#9733;</td><td>from the start</td></tr>
            <tr><td>carrot &middot; strawberry &middot; sunflower</td><td>&#9733;&#9733;</td><td>from the start</td></tr>
            <tr><td>midnight tulip &middot; tomato</td><td>&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</td><td>3 harvests</td></tr>
            <tr><td>pumpkin &middot; sweetcorn</td><td>&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</td><td>8 harvests</td></tr>
            <tr><td>golden wheat &middot; watermelon</td><td>&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</td><td>15 harvests</td></tr>
            <tr><td>grapevine &middot; pineapple &middot; prickly pear</td><td>&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</td><td>30 harvests &mdash; the exotic tier</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p>
          Stars mean two things: a living plant feeds the park by its stars, and starrier plants last longer
          between waterings. The strawberry and the grapevine <strong>regrow</strong> &mdash; three picks per plant.
        </p>
        <p>
          The park is the crossroads: <a href="/rave/">the rave</a> down the south road,
          <a href="/beach/">Banana Bay</a> out east &mdash; and everything you earn lands on
          <a href="/pass/">your pass</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="pkg__block" id="faq">
        <p class="pkg__kicker">questions</p>
        <h2>frequently asked</h2>
        <dl class="pkg__faq">
          <dt>Is The Park free to play?</dt>
          <dd>Yes &mdash; free, in the browser, no account. Your banana walks straight in through the gate.</dd>
          <dt>What do you do in The Park?</dt>
          <dd>Keep a shared garden alive: plant, water other people&rsquo;s beds, pull weeds, tidy, spot birds, hunt eggs. Everything nudges the health meter.</dd>
          <dt>What is park health?</dt>
          <dd>One number, 0&ndash;100, shared by everyone. It sinks on its own; tending pushes it back. A park nobody tends visibly dies.</dd>
          <dt>Can you play with other people?</dt>
          <dd>Yes &mdash; every banana is a real visitor, live, and the garden is shared. The meter is the whole park&rsquo;s score, not yours.</dd>
          <dt>How do you unlock better seeds?</dt>
          <dd>Harvest. Three harvests unlock three-star seeds, eight unlock four, fifteen unlock five &mdash; and thirty opens the six-star exotic tier.</dd>
          <dt>How do you get to The Park?</dt>
          <dd>Dress a banana in <a href="/make-a-banana/">the free builder</a> and walk in. The rave and the bay are one road away.</dd>
        </dl>
